summary:
- topic: Special Meeting Purpose
  text: The Superintendent explained that the special meeting was necessary to approve
    the budget articles ahead of the City Council's budget vote, due to an accelerated
    timeline this year compared to previous years.
- topic: Superintendent's Report
  text: The Superintendent announced the resignations of Erica Matio (Director of
    Curriculum), Samantha Matoya (Social Studies), and LB Murphy (Student Engagement
    Coordinator), thanking them for their service. He also promoted an upcoming community
    food drive.
- topic: FY26 Budget Action Items
  text: The Superintendent read all 19 budget action items into the record, covering
    the 11 cost centers, appropriations, local contributions, debt service, and capital
    improvement plan, totaling over $73 million.
- topic: Voting Procedure
  text: The Board agreed to a proposal by member DeAngelis to vote on the first budget
    item (Regular Instruction) separately and then vote on the remaining items in
    two large blocks to expedite the process.
- topic: Vote on Regular Instruction (Item 3.1)
  text: The board voted 4-2 to approve the Regular Instruction budget. Board member
    DeAngelis stated she was voting no to protest the cuts to social-emotional learning
    funding within that budget line.
- topic: Votes on Remaining Budget Items
  text: 'The board voted unanimously to approve the remaining budget items, which
    were bundled into two groups: cost centers 3.2-3.11 and action items 3.12-3.19.'
- topic: Board Comments
  text: Board members expressed appreciation for the administration and each other's
    work during a difficult budget process. Member DeAngelis noted that disagreement
    is a healthy part of representing the community, and the board was glad to move
    the budget forward to the City Council.
